From f8de8a67c689c79629391eb44eb0dd5d734d1b70 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 09:14:46 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] Mabar skins: offline LAN players see each other's skin
 and cape

Each phone announces its player's name and the SHA-1 of its skin and cape by UDP
broadcast on every network (hotspot included) and serves the PNGs over HTTP; the
others download them as they do an Ely.by skin. It runs only while a world is open
to LAN or the session is joined at a private address, and the URL's host is always
the announcement's sender.

